      {
         "id": "d",
         "prompt": "Let \\( w(x) = \\dfrac{x\\,f(x)}{g(x)} \\). Find \\( w'(3) \\), and write an equation for the line tangent to the graph of \\( w \\) at \\( x = 3 \\).",
         "setup_required": false,
         "answer_latex": "y = 6 - \\frac{29}{2}(x - 3)",
         "worked_solution": [
            {
               "text": "Differentiate the numerator x f(x) by the product rule and evaluate at x = 3.",
               "latex": "\\frac{d}{dx}\\left[ x\\,f(x) \\right] = f(x) + x\\,f'(x), \\quad f(3) + 3f'(3) = 4 + 3 = 7"
            },
            {
               "text": "Quotient rule at x = 3, with numerator value 3 f(3) = 12.",
               "latex": "w'(3) = \\frac{7 \\cdot 2 - 12 \\cdot 6}{2^{2}} = -\\frac{29}{2}"
            },
            {
               "text": "The point on the graph.",
               "latex": "w(3) = \\frac{12}{2} = 6"
            },
            {
               "text": "Tangent line.",
               "latex": "y = 6 - \\frac{29}{2}(x - 3)"
            }
